<aside class="install-security-note" aria-label="First-launch signing information">
<p class="section-copy">The current DMG contains an ad-hoc signed app. It is not Developer ID signed or notarized, so macOS may block first launch. Download from the official release link and verify its SHA256 before following the installer's README.</p>
<p class="section-copy">After installing the verified app in Applications, the README's first-launch command is:</p>
<pre class="install-command"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/ZackEyes.app</code></pre>
<p class="section-copy">Then open ZackEyes from Applications. Accessibility enables terminal tab jump; notification permission enables system alerts.</p>
</aside>
